Hour-by-hour tides, two states at once, calendar picker

Tides now draw a continuous curve. The stored highs and lows are
interpolated with a cosine, which is what the rule of twelfths
approximates, so the height at any minute comes out of data already
shipped. The chart shades legal shooting light, a scrubber reads the height
at any time, and a target height lists the times the tide passes it.

States are no longer either/or. NH and MA can be shown together, which is
what you want on the border: zone ids are namespaced per state, every
feature carries the state it came from, and tapping a spot adopts that
state for the rules. Season lookups take the state explicitly, so MA Sunday
closure and the merganser difference stay correct per side of the line.

The date face now opens the native calendar; the arrows still step a day.

